╭─ Patch Generation ───────────────────────────╮
│ Okay, I’ve realized the core issue. The      │
│ source-read event isn’t correctly            │
│ propagating changes to include files.        │
│ Sphinx’s include handling needs adjustment.  │
│ The problem isn’t with the extension itself, │
│ but with how Sphinx processes the include    │
│ directive and triggers the source-read       │
│ event. Specifically, the source-read event   │
│ isn't being reliably triggered for files     │
│ included via the include directive.          │
│                                              │
│ Here’s the patch:                            │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]<.../documentation/sphinx/yocto-vars  │
│  y[/file]                                    │
│  [original]                                  │
│  def setup(app: Sphinx):                     │
│      app.connect('source-read',              │
│  subst_vars_replace)                         │
│      return dict(                            │
│          version=__version__,                │
│          parallel_read_safe=True,            │
│          parallel_write_safe=True            │
│      )                                       │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]                                   │
│  def setup(app: Sphinx):                     │
│      app.connect('source-read',              │
│  subst_vars_replace)                         │
│      app.add_config_value('include-read-eve  │
│  ', True, 'builder')                         │
│      return dict(                            │
│          version=__version__,                │
│          parallel_read_safe=True,            │
│          parallel_write_safe=True            │
│      )                                       │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 2              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]<.../index.rst[/file]                 │
│  [original]                                  │
│  .. include:: something-to-include.rst       │
│  &REPLACE_ME;                                │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]                                   │
│  .. include:: something-to-include.rst       │
│  &REPLACE_ME;                                │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The yocto-vars.py file’s setup function      │
│ connects the subst_vars_replace function to  │
│ the source-read event. However, it doesn't   │
│ explicitly configure Sphinx to trigger the   │
│ source-read event for included files.  I've  │
│ added                                        │
│ app.add_config_value('include-read-event',   │
│ True, 'builder') to ensure that the          │
│ source-read event is triggered when an       │
│ include directive is encountered. This       │
│ should force Sphinx to process the included  │
│ file and trigger the extension's source-read │
│ handler. The index.rst file remains          │
│ unchanged as the issue lies in the Sphinx    │
│ configuration, not the include directive     │
│ itself. This change should ensure that the   │
│ subst_vars_replace function is called when   │
│ the included file is processed, allowing the │
│ replacement to occur.                        │
