│                                              │
│ Here's a breakdown of the investigation and  │
│ the API calls I'll make:                     │
│                                              │
│  1 Understand the source-read event: The     │
│    issue highlights that the source-read     │
│    event is connected to the                 │
│    subst_vars_replace function, which        │
│    modifies the source RST content.  We need │
│    to understand why this modification isn't │
│    propagating to the final HTML.            │
│  2 Inspect my-extension.py: The extension's  │
│    code is crucial. Let's examine how it     │
│    handles the source-read event and the     │
│    source data.                              │
│  3 Check the Sphinx configuration:  The      │
│    conf.py file might contain settings that  │
│    influence how Sphinx processes include    │
│    files.                                    │
│  4 Verify the include directive: The ..      │
│    include:: directive itself might be the   │
│    source of the problem.                    │
│                                              │
│ Based on these points, here's the sequence   │
│ of API calls I'll make:                      │
│                                              │
│  1 search_method_in_file(method_name='subst_ │
│    vars_replace',                            │
